    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\n`vi{` along with `vi[` (and possibly other commands) move the cursor ahead and select a block that the cursor is not inside, rather than highlighting the block that the cursor is within. This is more easily explained with a screen recording:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/54135831/4d889de9-2257-4ed7-a099-1ced74b3f662\r\n\r\nIs this a bug? If not, is there some way for me to use the default Neovim/Vim behaviour while still using this plugin?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the following commands to create a minimal installation of `mini.ai` and an example file to test the behaviour described:\r\n```sh\r\ncat >> minimal.lua << EOF\r\nlocal mini_path = \"./mini-ai\"\r\n\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\r\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installing mini.ai...\" | redraw')\r\n  local clone_cmd = {\r\n    \"git\",\r\n    \"clone\",\r\n    \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n    \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.ai.git\",\r\n    mini_path,\r\n  }\r\n  vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\r\n  vim.cmd('echo \"Installation finished\" | redraw')\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini-ai/lua/mini/ai\").setup({})\r\nEOF\r\n```\r\n\r\n```sh\r\ncat >> test.txt << EOF\r\nfoo = {\r\n  bar: 1, \r\n  qux: { a: 2 },\r\n  baz: 3\r\n}\r\nEOF\r\n```\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nnvim -nu minimal.lua test.txt\r\n```\r\nNeovim will open. Move your cursor to `qux` and type `vi{` in normal mode. The block highlighted will be ` a: 2 `.\r\n\r\nThen, run\r\n\r\n```\r\nnvim --clean test.txt\r\n```\r\n\r\nto open the same file without `mini.ai`, and repeat the process of moving to `qux` and typing `vi{`. The highlighted block will go from `bar: 1` to `baz: 3`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nSee screen recording above",
