            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski sorry to revive this thread, but I've been playing around with the options a little more - would you be open to adding a version of `cover_or_next` that first searches for a covering span and only looks ahead for a next span if no covering span exists, which would more closely match the default behaviour of Vim? Alternatively, would you be happy for me to contribute this in a PR?\r\n> \r\n> No worries if not, just thought I'd check!\r\n\r\nIt already does that. The difference is that it first does that in current line first.\r\n\r\nThe suggested approach to resolving this is still the one from [this commit](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/790#issuecomment-2045602383). I.e. use `'serach_method = 'cover'` and use explicit variants `in`/`an`/`il`/`al` when you want next or previous match.",
